+# F2 geometry cost diagnostic reproduction
+
+Apply this patch to commit 67ba321a2abf4dc117013d75450e56023713e088 in an isolated source checkout. It adds the reviewed observer and the exact driver/witness tool bytes used for the retained study. It does not change solver selection or scientific acceptance.
+
+For witness reproduction, copy this directory's five tool files into a fresh scratch directory, with the patched checkout available there as `f2-geometry-source`. Compile `f2_geometry_feature_probe.rs` with Rust 1.85.1, edition 2021 and optimization; run `f2_geometry_feature_tests.py` with Python assertions enabled. The script enforces `sys.flags.optimize == 0`. This is the original eight geometry fixtures plus two admission fixtures; no estimation is involved.
+
+For native cost reproduction, build the patched source using the standard Linux build script, the generic `-C target-cpu=x86-64` configuration and `FEREG_F2_GEOMETRY=1`. Keep default release features and the existing runtime FMA table. The standard build audit, loader and numeric guard checks remain required.
+
+The frozen pricing driver takes explicit source, plugin, harness, input bindings, prior checkpoint reference, evidence manifest, case and output paths. Use its `--help` interface. Its original six Auto requests are the three retained OLS three-effect cases at one and sixteen workers, with one call per cell, 120 seconds per call, 600 seconds total and no retries. It is SCC-only and requires a sixteen-slot allocation. Reconstruct existing frozen cases from their original campaign DTAs only; verify complete case, source and column hashes. The campaign evidence and exact Auto anchors are retained in `bench/results/fable-20261011-discovery.json` and the input evidence it binds.
+
+A new reproduction must create its own reviewed hash manifest and artifact identities after reproducing the independent witnesses. Original log/result hashes in the retained evidence identify the completed observation; new clock values and build hashes cannot be expected to reproduce those captures. No raw log or generated case is embedded in this patch.
+
+Interpret primary and final-residual observer clocks separately. The current diagnostic computes features twice; a future selector could avoid geometry when an unchanged initial certificate already passes. No cache or selector is implemented. The bound is for exact arithmetic, true unit weights and one shared global constant; it is not a floating-point convergence guarantee or an LSMR iteration predictor. A new native experiment requires its own explicit approval and budget.
